WEBVTT

00:01.450 --> 00:03.970
Blessings from God in Heaven.

00:03.970 --> 00:06.230
Divine protection from the Spirit of the earth.

00:06.750 --> 00:09.310
Listen to God's Word 
that whispers within the wind,

00:09.710 --> 00:14.070
and chew upon the benevolence of 
the spirits as the sheep chews on grass.

00:16.580 --> 00:21.580
The shepherd guides the sheep, 
and God guides the shepherd.

00:22.250 --> 00:27.080
The shepherd walks down the righteous path 
through God's providence.

00:31.460 --> 00:35.680
Spice and Wolf

00:35.680 --> 00:36.800
Spice and Wolf

00:36.800 --> 00:42.140
Spice and Wolf

02:00.780 --> 02:03.260
We apologize for suspecting you.

02:03.010 --> 02:08.270
<b>Episode 8
Fellow Traveler 
and Foreboding News</b>

02:03.260 --> 02:05.520
You must be a good shepherd.

02:05.980 --> 02:08.690
May I ask the shepherd 
we have met through divine providence

02:08.690 --> 02:11.310
to pray for the safety of our journey?

02:12.970 --> 02:14.230
I would be happy to.

02:16.570 --> 02:19.600
Palti mis tuelo moro.

02:19.600 --> 02:22.620
Lu spinzzio tilatto kul.

02:33.850 --> 02:35.400
Thank you very much.

02:35.400 --> 02:37.800
No, thank you.

02:43.970 --> 02:44.810
Well, then.

02:45.300 --> 02:49.140
Um, are you heading toward Ruvinheigen?

02:49.490 --> 02:52.060
Yes, we came from Poroson.

02:52.060 --> 02:55.020
Why did you take this road? I mean...

02:55.890 --> 02:58.360
did you not hear about the wolves?

02:58.360 --> 02:59.820
We did.

02:59.820 --> 03:02.070
It's just that we're pressed for time.

03:02.070 --> 03:03.410
I see.

03:04.290 --> 03:05.420
Is there something wrong?

03:05.420 --> 03:06.100
Huh?

03:06.100 --> 03:07.750
Oh, no...

03:07.750 --> 03:09.340
Well...

03:09.340 --> 03:10.350
Please don't hold back.

03:10.860 --> 03:13.140
Or could it be there's something you need?

03:13.630 --> 03:15.790
Well,

03:17.350 --> 03:21.380
I was wondering if you would be 
interested in hiring me...

03:22.500 --> 03:28.300
Well, as you can see, we're traveling 
merchants and have no sheep.

03:29.060 --> 03:31.100
Though I appreciate the offer...

03:31.100 --> 03:33.440
N-No, that's not what I mean.

03:33.750 --> 03:35.740
I am a shepherd.

03:35.740 --> 03:40.030
Um, I can drive wolves 
away as well as raise sheep.

03:44.110 --> 03:49.870
If you hire me, I can keep the wolves 
at bay during your journey.

03:55.390 --> 03:56.780
So...

03:56.780 --> 03:58.380
What do you think?

04:04.820 --> 04:06.850
What do you think about that shepherd?

04:06.850 --> 04:10.040
Hmm. I am cuter.

04:10.040 --> 04:12.380
I'm not talking about that. 
I'm asking about her skill.

04:12.380 --> 04:13.140
Her skills?

04:13.440 --> 04:16.000
How are her skills as a shepherd?

04:16.000 --> 04:17.710
You were listening, weren't you?

04:17.710 --> 04:20.140
You have me.

04:20.140 --> 04:21.940
Of course I do.

04:21.940 --> 04:24.740
It's just that she could lead us 
to new business opportunities.

04:30.660 --> 04:34.000
Oh. It's not like I'm being 
swayed by her beauty.

04:36.070 --> 04:38.000
After all, you're much cuter than her.

04:47.930 --> 04:50.090
Though barely, you pass.

04:50.870 --> 04:52.620
So, how are her skills?

04:52.620 --> 04:54.600
I would be able to hunt her sheep.

04:54.600 --> 04:59.480
But she would easily keep normal wolves 
at bay, even if they attacked all at once.

04:59.840 --> 05:02.280
She has excellent dog-handling skills.

05:02.280 --> 05:09.700
Troublesome shepherds have clever 
dogs and work with them as one.

05:10.190 --> 05:12.740
So young. I fear how much 
she will grow in the future.

05:13.430 --> 05:15.500
Perhaps I should nip the bud...

05:15.500 --> 05:17.030
Got it. Thanks.

05:17.580 --> 05:18.410
Hey.

05:18.410 --> 05:19.120
Hm?

05:19.120 --> 05:21.170
Are you truly hiring her?

05:23.940 --> 05:26.320
Do you hate shepherds that much?

05:26.320 --> 05:28.970
If it were a matter of liking her
 or not, then I don't.

05:28.970 --> 05:30.220
However, I meant something else.

05:30.550 --> 05:33.370
I was asking if you are 
truly all right with that.

05:33.790 --> 05:34.930
What do you mean?

05:34.930 --> 05:38.730
If you hire her, 
we will be traveling together.

05:39.000 --> 05:40.710
You have no problem with that?

05:41.120 --> 05:44.490
Well, it'll take about two days 
to reach Ruvinheigen.

05:45.290 --> 05:46.030
No good?

05:46.030 --> 05:48.650
That is not what I am saying.

05:48.650 --> 05:51.420
Sorry, you'll have to bear 
with it for a little while.

05:51.420 --> 05:53.580
What must I bear?

05:54.180 --> 05:56.150
Well, I mean...

05:56.150 --> 06:00.380
I just want to see if a shepherd can 
really guard us against the wolves.

06:00.870 --> 06:02.540
You can handle two days, right?

06:03.730 --> 06:07.130
That is fine, but that is not the main problem.

06:07.500 --> 06:09.900
Well, that's true...

06:09.900 --> 06:14.500
If we carelessly travel with others, will not 
the risk of being discovered increase?

06:16.600 --> 06:18.450
I see.

06:18.450 --> 06:22.690
You probably wished 
to hear something like this?

06:24.530 --> 06:28.650
"I wished for the two of us to travel alone..."

06:31.570 --> 06:32.530
Fool.

06:33.750 --> 06:35.770
No, I...

06:35.770 --> 06:37.120
Goodness.

06:37.120 --> 06:40.250
Well, two days should 
not pose much of a problem.

06:43.170 --> 06:44.820
I apologize for making you wait.

06:44.820 --> 06:45.750
Not at all.

06:46.100 --> 06:47.300
U-Um...

06:47.300 --> 06:49.220
How about forty Trie?

06:49.220 --> 06:52.640
We'll pay an additional fee 
if you fend off any wolf attacks.

06:53.860 --> 06:55.620
Th-Thank you very much.

06:55.620 --> 06:56.640
No, thank <i>you</i>.

06:57.140 --> 06:59.480
May I ask your name?

06:59.480 --> 07:01.440
Oh, I-I'm sorry.

07:04.230 --> 07:05.860
I'm Nora Arendt.

07:12.780 --> 07:13.700
Enek.

07:17.210 --> 07:19.080
Have you been herding sheep for a long time?

07:19.080 --> 07:21.290
I've only done it for about four years.

07:21.290 --> 07:24.970
Did you raise your sheepdog, 
um, Enek, yourself?

07:24.970 --> 07:26.960
No, I found him.

07:27.280 --> 07:30.860
Enek is the reason I became a shepherd.

07:30.860 --> 07:31.880
And until then?

07:33.230 --> 07:36.560
I lived in a shelter for the poor.

07:37.830 --> 07:39.080
I see.

07:39.080 --> 07:43.980
But I've always wanted to have a job of my own.

07:47.730 --> 07:50.550
I was fortunate enough to meet Enek.

07:51.090 --> 07:54.840
He was ragged and covered 
in wounds when I met him.

07:54.840 --> 07:55.780
Was it wolves?

07:56.250 --> 07:59.240
No, I think it was mountain 
bandits or mercenaries...

07:59.580 --> 08:04.460
He had this staff in his mouth and was 
cowering under a small cliff on a hill.

08:04.810 --> 08:05.870
I see.

08:06.290 --> 08:11.290
But, this was the first time a shepherd 
offered to guard me on my journey.

08:11.290 --> 08:11.960
Huh?

08:11.960 --> 08:15.460
Normal shepherds don't do such things.

08:15.460 --> 08:18.060
Um, well...

08:18.060 --> 08:18.640
Huh?

08:19.040 --> 08:22.100
I wanted someone to talk to...

08:24.970 --> 08:26.460
I understand that feeling.

08:26.460 --> 08:27.790
And...

08:28.400 --> 08:31.850
I want to become a tailor.

08:31.850 --> 08:34.200
So, you need money for the association fees?

08:34.570 --> 08:39.750
That's true. You would earn more money 
guarding merchants than tending sheep.

08:39.750 --> 08:41.960
I'm sure that it's difficult 
to fight over territory.

08:41.960 --> 08:43.410
That's true.

08:43.710 --> 08:48.130
The safer areas have already been 
taken by other shepherds.

08:48.130 --> 08:51.650
So, the only areas left 
are filled with wolves...

08:51.650 --> 08:52.550
Yes.

08:52.930 --> 08:55.100
Wolves are very troublesome.

09:02.330 --> 09:04.980
On top of that, they're 
cunning and underhanded.

09:04.980 --> 09:09.680
They may be listening in on us, 
so I wouldn't bad mouth them.

09:09.680 --> 09:10.630
Right.

09:12.020 --> 09:15.240
Um, I'm sorry. I will need to 
settle down for the day...

09:15.240 --> 09:17.280
Oh, I forgot.

09:17.280 --> 09:19.490
It's already the time for shepherds to rest.

09:19.490 --> 09:20.680
Yes.

09:20.680 --> 09:25.540
I have to sleep now in order to 
watch over the sheep at night.

09:25.540 --> 09:28.010
Then, we will set up camp here.

09:34.810 --> 09:39.600
You're skilled enough 
to handle a lot more sheep.

09:39.600 --> 09:43.600
No, I'm happy for any small amount of work.

09:43.890 --> 09:46.340
I can't take care of that many...

09:46.340 --> 09:49.270
Your employer probably lacks a discerning eye.

09:49.890 --> 09:52.130
Why not change your employer?

09:52.130 --> 09:52.850
Huh?

09:52.850 --> 09:54.250
Change my employer?

09:54.990 --> 09:57.560
I couldn't possibly...

09:57.560 --> 10:02.580
Sorry. As a merchant, I can't help 
calculating things based on loss and profit.

10:02.580 --> 10:04.190
Oh, n-no...

10:07.420 --> 10:08.870
Um...

10:08.870 --> 10:09.630
Yes?

10:09.630 --> 10:15.670
Um, is it common to change employers?

10:18.470 --> 10:22.250
Pardon me for asking, 
but is the Church your employer?

10:22.250 --> 10:22.890
Huh?

10:22.890 --> 10:24.410
Y-Yes.

10:26.460 --> 10:29.810
The Church offers steady work, doesn't it?

10:30.820 --> 10:31.870
Yes.

10:32.350 --> 10:34.360
I am truly fortunate.

10:34.360 --> 10:36.930
The Church entrusted their sheep to me,

10:36.930 --> 10:40.360
and they've also been quite considerate of me.

10:40.770 --> 10:41.910
I see.

10:42.580 --> 10:46.560
If that's the case, there's probably 
no need for you to change employers.

10:46.560 --> 10:48.100
Is that so?

10:48.100 --> 10:48.790
Yes.

10:48.790 --> 10:51.490
The pay may be lower,

10:51.890 --> 10:56.210
but the Church will exist 
as long as God doesn't abandon us.

10:56.500 --> 11:00.130
At the very least, you will not be out 
of a job and have no food to eat.

11:02.630 --> 11:04.380
You're right...

11:05.700 --> 11:11.020
Well, I'll tell the merchants I know 
in Ruvinheigen about you, Ms. Nora.

11:12.390 --> 11:16.230
God never forbade 
having another job on the side.

11:17.970 --> 11:19.390
Thank you!

11:29.580 --> 11:31.290
Looks like a difficult job.

11:31.670 --> 11:34.670
Well, daily tail maintenance is important.

11:35.780 --> 11:39.510
Oh, you were talking about that young girl.

11:42.090 --> 11:44.150
Her name is Nora Arendt.

11:48.820 --> 11:49.890
H-Hey, now!

11:54.290 --> 11:56.850
That's why I asked you first!

11:56.850 --> 12:00.000
I cannot even groom my tail in peace.

12:00.000 --> 12:01.320
Couldn't you do it in the wagon?

12:02.290 --> 12:03.990
If I had groomed myself in the wagon...

12:04.320 --> 12:05.490
If you had?

12:06.410 --> 12:09.980
The two of you seemed to have a nice chat.

12:09.980 --> 12:12.320
Well, she wanted to talk to someone.

12:12.320 --> 12:14.170
There wasn't a reason to refuse her, was there?

12:14.660 --> 12:18.250
And I hadn't spoken to 
a normal girl in a while...

12:18.250 --> 12:22.800
You did not even notice that 
she disliked speaking with you.

12:22.800 --> 12:23.840
Huh?

12:30.500 --> 12:32.430
Well, that's fine, too.

12:34.570 --> 12:36.420
If I was loved at first sight,

12:36.420 --> 12:39.780
I'd miss the pleasure of experiencing 
someone's affection for me grow.

12:44.490 --> 12:46.770
Aren't I a pretty smooth talker?

12:51.950 --> 12:54.330
H-How unlike you!

12:57.790 --> 13:01.010
Hey, you're laughing too much.

13:01.380 --> 13:02.230
Jeez...

13:10.460 --> 13:12.130
What a good laugh.

13:13.510 --> 13:14.820
Do you feel better now?

13:14.820 --> 13:18.360
Yes. You have quite a surprising trump card.

13:18.360 --> 13:21.690
Well, I'm happy as long as 
your bad mood is gone.

13:21.690 --> 13:23.530
Hm? Bad mood?

13:23.530 --> 13:27.080
You were in a bad mood because 
you couldn't groom your tail.

13:27.080 --> 13:30.450
Oh, that is right.

13:30.450 --> 13:32.120
It cannot be helped.

13:32.120 --> 13:36.380
I laughed so much that it seems foolish 
to care about such things.

13:37.590 --> 13:39.000
Is that so?

13:39.000 --> 13:40.310
I should start collecting firewood.

13:41.530 --> 13:43.140
Hey, you.

13:43.630 --> 13:45.030
Wh-What is it?

13:45.550 --> 13:50.100
Some raw sheep would be nice 
every once in a while.

13:50.420 --> 13:52.060
What do you think?

14:00.670 --> 14:03.290
If you're going to joke, say something 
that I can actually laugh about.

14:10.210 --> 14:11.450
Over there.

14:23.230 --> 14:25.130
Here is your promised forty Trie.

14:25.870 --> 14:29.430
But these coins are actually
 worth more than that...

14:29.430 --> 14:30.930
It's an investment.

14:30.930 --> 14:32.470
Investment?

14:32.470 --> 14:35.290
If I become acquainted with a skilled shepherd,

14:35.290 --> 14:39.290
I might gain some surprising money-making 
opportunities when trading wool.

14:43.350 --> 14:45.150
Thank you very much.

14:45.570 --> 14:49.290
Are you only able to guard people 
going through the road we just traveled?

14:49.290 --> 14:52.820
Um, I can go as far as Kasrata and Poroson.

14:52.820 --> 14:54.990
Oh, and Lamtra as well.

14:54.990 --> 14:56.100
Lamtra?

14:56.510 --> 14:58.690
You either have to go through 
a dangerous forest

14:58.690 --> 15:01.580
or make a very large detour to reach that town.

15:01.580 --> 15:03.490
I'm not talking about the detour.

15:03.490 --> 15:06.340
I can accept requests 
through the forest as well.

15:06.340 --> 15:07.670
That's amazing.

15:08.040 --> 15:11.050
It's a place that's so dangerous they say 
that even knights tremble in fear.

15:11.050 --> 15:14.890
If you can go as far as Lamtra, 
you have a good chance of finding customers.

15:14.890 --> 15:16.840
Thank you very much for your help.

15:16.840 --> 15:20.180
Well, then. We'll be entering from that gate.

15:26.140 --> 15:30.060
Now, I wonder how those 
honey-pickled peaches will taste.

15:30.500 --> 15:32.320
I cannot wait.

15:32.320 --> 15:33.530
You still remember that?

15:33.530 --> 15:36.180
Do you plan to go back on your word?

15:36.180 --> 15:38.160
I can't buy it if it's not for sale.

15:38.710 --> 15:40.330
Of course.

16:15.580 --> 16:16.740
Pass permit.

16:16.740 --> 16:17.610
Here it is.

16:18.850 --> 16:21.540
From Poroson? What did you bring?

16:22.250 --> 16:24.210
Twenty sets of armor.

16:24.480 --> 16:27.250
Armor? From Poroson?

16:27.250 --> 16:28.880
Y-Yes.

16:28.880 --> 16:32.100
I purchased them from Latparron 
Trading. Is there something wrong?

16:32.880 --> 16:36.550
Yes, this looks like 
the type of armor they carry.

16:36.550 --> 16:39.890
Do you wish to pay the taxes 
with cash or actual goods?

16:39.890 --> 16:40.870
With actual goods.

16:42.080 --> 16:43.770
That's a wise decision.

16:44.250 --> 16:46.970
Pay with one set of armor over there.

16:48.740 --> 16:51.440
Is armor from Poroson rare?

16:51.440 --> 16:54.900
No. This city is always in need of armor.

16:54.900 --> 16:57.990
A lot of the armor should be 
imported from Poroson.

17:00.790 --> 17:01.890
Thank you.

17:05.490 --> 17:06.500
Is there a problem?

17:06.770 --> 17:08.230
No, it's nothing.

17:15.450 --> 17:18.050
Government officials are unpleasant 
no matter where one goes.

17:18.360 --> 17:21.780
They seem to dislike the idea of 
a mere traveling merchant

17:21.780 --> 17:23.430
earning a large amount of money.

17:26.580 --> 17:27.850
Well, it's fine.

17:27.850 --> 17:30.580
We just need to sell these 
and rake in our profits.

17:30.580 --> 17:31.390
Yes!

17:31.860 --> 17:33.370
By the way.

17:33.370 --> 17:34.100
What is it?

17:34.100 --> 17:35.710
I have grown hungry.

17:49.820 --> 17:51.140
Delicious!

17:56.590 --> 17:58.150
Another serving!

17:58.150 --> 17:59.470
Appreciate the business!

17:59.990 --> 18:01.810
Here you go! Two beers!

18:01.810 --> 18:03.330
The alcohol is delicious.

18:03.330 --> 18:06.570
What a nice and lively town! Do you not agree?

18:06.570 --> 18:09.270
In exchange, you can't let 
your guard down here.

18:09.660 --> 18:13.110
Don't get into trouble with 
the knights and mercenaries here.

18:13.110 --> 18:14.980
No problem!

18:18.310 --> 18:19.530
Where are we going?

18:19.990 --> 18:21.380
The trading house.

18:22.700 --> 18:24.250
Hey, you have something around your mouth.

18:30.540 --> 18:33.890
Geez! You better remember this!

18:33.890 --> 18:35.350
However...

18:36.200 --> 18:38.510
What is the point of me going with you?

18:38.510 --> 18:41.510
I would like to continue 
drinking in the square.

18:42.770 --> 18:44.510
It'd be dangerous to leave you alone.

18:46.300 --> 18:48.810
Yes. I am cute!

18:49.330 --> 18:51.790
It is dangerous to leave me alone.

18:53.090 --> 18:57.490
You can't sway all the soldiers of the Church 
and holy knights with your cuteness.

18:57.490 --> 19:00.570
I can't have you getting drunk 
and showing your ears and tail in public.

19:00.570 --> 19:03.740
Then, we would only make virtue of necessity.

19:04.150 --> 19:07.340
I would take you in my mouth 
and escape out of town.

19:10.830 --> 19:13.760
I heard your daughter 
has recovered from being sick?

19:13.760 --> 19:16.860
Yes, truly a blessing from God.

19:16.860 --> 19:19.580
My husband hasn't been 
feeling well lately, either.

19:19.580 --> 19:23.940
That's terrible. You should have the priest 
pray for him as soon as possible.

19:23.940 --> 19:26.560
The Church is the only thing 
you can really believe in.

19:27.060 --> 19:29.360
So, what is a trading house?

19:29.360 --> 19:32.980
Running a business is fraught 
with dangers and accidents.

19:32.980 --> 19:35.810
Knights protect themselves with armor,

19:35.810 --> 19:38.890
but we merchants protect ourselves 
with our connections to other people.

19:38.890 --> 19:41.070
That's what we call a merchant association.

19:42.590 --> 19:45.740
I'm part of a merchant association that 
consists of merchants from my homeland.

19:46.190 --> 19:48.340
The trading house here is 
a branch of that association.

19:48.340 --> 19:51.030
It's like my home away from home.

19:57.050 --> 19:59.360
Okay. Wait here.

19:59.360 --> 20:00.760
What?

20:00.760 --> 20:04.570
Were you not planning to take me in
and show me off to your fellows?

20:04.570 --> 20:06.930
I'd have to marry you first for that.

20:07.260 --> 20:10.620
My homeland's wedding celebration
 is pretty rough. Still want to enter?

20:11.700 --> 20:13.050
I'll be quick.

20:13.050 --> 20:15.540
I'll buy you some sweet bread 
if you wait here obediently.

20:15.990 --> 20:17.730
Do not treat me as a child!

20:18.290 --> 20:19.440
Then, you don't want the bread?

20:19.440 --> 20:20.150
I do.

20:24.030 --> 20:27.030
Oh, looks like an incompetent 
merchant is visiting.

20:27.320 --> 20:32.660
Anyone who comes around this time 
isn't serious about making money.

20:32.660 --> 20:37.630
A great merchant can make money 
without collecting any dust on his shoes.

20:38.180 --> 20:41.510
He only dirties his fingertips 
with a bit of black ink.

20:41.510 --> 20:45.620
Running around the market all day long is 
what third-class merchants do.

20:45.620 --> 20:46.890
Am I wrong?

20:50.510 --> 20:53.490
You've become a smooth talker.

20:53.490 --> 20:56.690
Welcome home, my son!

20:57.020 --> 20:59.700
Please stop calling me your son.

20:59.700 --> 21:01.650
What are you talking about?!

21:01.650 --> 21:07.120
Every member of the Rowen Merchant 
Association is my son or daughter!

21:07.120 --> 21:13.410
On top of that, I know that you often 
wet your bed when camping outside.

21:13.410 --> 21:17.040
Want me to remind you of the time 
you snatched the proceeds of a sale

21:17.040 --> 21:19.880
to go to a brothel with 
your friends, all while trembling?

21:19.880 --> 21:22.260
Okay! Okay!

21:22.730 --> 21:27.630
I am Kraft Lawrence, the son of 
the great Jacob Tarantino!

21:28.350 --> 21:30.180
Well, Kraft.

21:30.780 --> 21:34.980
It's been a year since you've 
come back to your home in Ruvinheigen!

21:45.150 --> 21:46.990
Is this the Remerio Trading Company?

21:47.410 --> 21:50.640
Yes. What is your business here?

21:50.640 --> 21:53.200
Did a merchant named Lawrence visit here?

21:54.590 --> 21:59.630
